# server/Dockerfile's build context (docker-compose.yml's `engine` and
# `local-proxy` services, context: ".") only ever COPYs server/{content,
# engine,gateway,webclient} and sdk/ - see its COPY list. Everything else
# below is either dead weight (node_modules, .git - ~750MB+ combined without
# this file) or live host state that must never leave the host at all (the
# manager's sqlite db, bot credentials in bots/*/bot.env).
#
# Nested node_modules matter doubly: left in, COPY server/engine (etc.) would
# layer the host's macOS/arm64-built node_modules on top of the image's own
# `bun install` (done earlier, for Linux) - the opposite of what that
# dependency-layer caching is for.

.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
/data
/bots
/manager
/mcp
/db
/tasks
/wiki
/learnings
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
**/.DS_Store

# Build artifacts regenerated inside the image anyway (server/Dockerfile runs
# `bun run build` for both the webclient and engine itself).
server/webclient/out
server/engine/dist
manager/web/dist
